Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-563):
/usr/bin/bzdiff:51:4: warning[SC2034]: F appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally).
#   49|                   case "$2" in
#   50|   	        *.bz2)
#   51|-> 			F=`echo "$2" | sed 's|.*/||;s|.bz2$||'`
#   52|   			tmp=`mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/bzdiff.XXXXXXXXXX` || {
#   53|   			      echo 'cannot create a temporary file' >&2
F is assigned but never read in this version of bzdiff, so the dead assignment cannot affect behaviour.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-398):
/usr/bin/bzgrep:58:28: error[SC1075]: Use 'elif' instead of 'else if' (or put 'if' on new line if nesting).
#   56|   res=0
#   57|   for i do
#   58|->   if test -f "$i"; then :; else if test -f "$i.bz2"; then i="$i.bz2"; fi; fi
#   59|     if test $list -eq 1; then
#   60|       bzip2 -cdfq "$i" | $grep $opt "$pat" 2>&1 > /dev/null && echo $i
The inner 'if' is terminated by its own 'fi' on the same line, which makes the construct equivalent to 'elif'; changing it would be cosmetic only.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-783):
/usr/bin/bzgrep:60:42: warning[SC2069]: To redirect stdout+stderr, 2>&1 must be last (or use '{ cmd > file; } 2>&1' to clarify).
#   58|     if test -f "$i"; then :; else if test -f "$i.bz2"; then i="$i.bz2"; fi; fi
#   59|     if test $list -eq 1; then
#   60|->     bzip2 -cdfq "$i" | $grep $opt "$pat" 2>&1 > /dev/null && echo $i
#   61|       r=$?
#   62|     elif test $# -eq 1 -o $silent -eq 1; then
The redirection order is deliberate: 2>&1 keeps error messages on the terminal and sends only the matching output to /dev/null.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-156):
/usr/bin/bzgrep:74:10: warning[SC2046]: Quote this to prevent word splitting.
#   72|       # r=${PIPESTATUS[1]}
#   73|       exec 3>&1
#   74|->     eval `
#   75|         exec 4>&1 >&3 3>&-
#   76|         {
The substitution feeds a block of shell code to eval, which re-joins its arguments and parses them again, so the split is harmless and quoting would change nothing.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-456):
/usr/bin/bzmore:11:5: warning[SC2209]: Use var=$(command) to assign output (or quote to assign string).
#    9|   case "$prog" in
#   10|   	*less)	more=less	;;
#   11|-> 	*)	more=more       ;;
#   12|   esac
#   13|   
The assignment stores the literal pager name 'more' in a variable; no command substitution is missing here.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING:
/usr/bin/bzmore:14:16: warning[SC3037]: In POSIX sh, echo flags are undefined.
#   12|   esac
#   13|   
#   14|-> if test "`echo -n a`" = "-n a"; then
#   15|     # looks like a SysV system:
#   16|     n1=''; n2='\c'
This line is the echo -n capability probe itself: it tests how the local echo treats flags, so the non-POSIX usage is intentional.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-398):
/usr/bin/bzmore:28:48: warning[SC2172]: Trapping signals by number is not well defined. Prefer signal names.
#   26|   fi
#   27|   if test $? -eq 0 -a -n "$oldtty"; then
#   28|->    trap 'stty $oldtty 2>/dev/null; exit' 0 2 3 5 10 13 15
#   29|   else
#   30|      trap 'stty $ncb echo 2>/dev/null; exit' 0 2 3 5 10 13 15
Avoid fixing them to be cautious that a fix won't introduce a new compatibility issue on other operating systems.

